leigh: quick note from canary for raven-q2-v1: streaming funcall parse errors ~1.9% on 5k calls, sync fine.
nana: only streaming?
leigh: yes. captured sample shows trailing closers merged into next chunk: ```
{"tool":"search","args":{"q":"sourdough"}}

{"tool":"open_url","args":{"url":"http://ex.com/rec"}}

]}
```
nana: looks like chunk boundary mid-structure. hypothesis: quantization changed tokenization so splits moved.
ci-bot: canary raven-q2-v1 started at 1760004200 cfg: stream_chunk=512 kv_cache=on
leigh: tried a fallback: on parse fail, attempt small salvage by wrapping joined non-empty chunks in array and json.loads. reduced failures to 0.5% in trial.
nana: add unit tests for truncated suffix and interleaved tools, plus semantic eval to ensure no accidental merges. log raw stream for audits.
leigh: will open PR behind flag for q2 family, monitor parsed_tool_count and semantic-eval for 48h. :eyes:
